    "type": "bay",
    "island": "st_john",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "Waterlemon Bay; Intlentution ?4 mile wide, between Annaberg Point and Leinster Point, on north shore of St. John I. : partially inclosed by Waterlemon Cay. It affords surf bathing and anchorage for small craft 200 yards from Waterlemon Cay. Bottom is of white sand, carpeted with brilliantly -- 199 of 215 196 u. s. COAST AND ~EODETIO BTJRVEIP colored, gracefully formed marine plants. Named I' Leinster Bay, \" on T. 3722, Dan. 265, B. A. 2452, H. 0. 3903 : correctly, 88 ehown by proximity of Estate, Point, and Hill, of same name. . Dan; 80 and Derrotero extend the name Leinster Bay to include the whole indentation otherwise known as Brim Bay. West-India Pilot and Zabriskie erroneously shift name Lelnster Bay to west arm of whole indentation described, better known as Mary Creek. Same as Waterlimon Bay. -Oxholm.",
